        "date": "2026-11-25T21:50:28Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): keep the custom-limit refusal, pin the trochoidal clean-up check\n\nReview fixes for PR #4008 (head b05f1318c):\n\n1. Restore main's whole-path refusal for a custom max_engagement. The\n   clean-up check only steps the peel down first. Decision in\n   docs/decisions/3849-trochoidal-cleanup-engagement.md.\n2. No expect() or unchecked index in the clean-up check: the baseline is\n   a plain value, the first chain point is read with first().\n3. End-to-end pins: a 2D and a 3D Trochoidal operation on a notch pocket\n   carry Warning::EngagementExceeded in the cached warnings.\n4. Step-down pins: wide 30x24 D6 and L-shape D10 at 60 deg step down,\n   post, carry the \"peel step was reduced\" note and no warning.\n5. A pin that is red on upstream/main: the notch pocket at the 90 deg\n   default (118.5 deg on main, no note). The test comment is corrected.\n6. The warning names the clean-up feed through the measured peak (the\n   note carries the level Z), not the first lane cut.\n\nThe check and its notes move to adaptive_troch_check.rs (400-line rule).\n\nRefs #3849\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
